cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "airct-benchmark: PubMed E-utilities pipeline of the AI-RCT Benchmark study"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Wito85/airct-benchmark"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22299272
url: "https://osf.io/qkb9g/"
abstract: >-
  Pipeline of the preregistered bibliometric meta-research study "Randomized trial share of
  medical artificial intelligence literature benchmarked against established clinical fields"
  (OSF registration DOI 10.17605/OSF.IO/QKB9G). The package retrieves PubMed record counts for a
  fixed catalogue of 2,034 queries (publication years 2015 to 2024) through the NCBI E-utilities
  twice in one session on the registered freeze date, retrieves PMID lists and efetch XML for the
  RCT-tagged and enriched untagged strata of artificial intelligence and stroke in 2024, draws the
  seeded validation samples, extracts trial registration identifiers, and writes SHA-256 manifests.
  Every query string is copied character for character from item Q12 of the registration.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - randomized controlled trials
  - bibliometrics
  - meta-research
  - PubMed
  - MeSH
  - preregistration
